+salt.cache.sqlite3_cache
+========================
+
+A durable, single-file cache backend built on the Python standard
+library's :mod:`sqlite3 <python:sqlite3>` module. Useful for single-node
+masters that want the minion data cache to survive a master restart
+without running a separate database service.
+
+.. automodule:: salt.cache.sqlite3_cache
+    :members:
diff --git a/doc/ref/configuration/master.rst b/doc/ref/configuration/master.rst
index b1d4844..2a56093 100644
--- a/doc/ref/configuration/master.rst
+++ b/doc/ref/configuration/master.rst
@@ -914,6 +914,14 @@ Cache subsystem module to use for minion data cache.  Common values:
   matching can run **orders of magnitude faster** than ``localfs``.
   Migrate existing data with ``salt-run cache.migrate``.  See
   :ref:`mmap-cache` for benchmarks, sizing, and durability notes.
+* ``sqlite3`` — durable single-file backend using only the Python standard
+  library's :mod:`sqlite3 <python:sqlite3>` module.  No extra service to
+  install; cached data (grains, mine data, job returns, etc.) survives a
+  master restart.  Good fit for single-node masters that want durability
+  without operating Redis or MySQL.  The database file defaults to
+  ``salt_cache.sqlite3`` under :conf_master:`cachedir` and can be
+  overridden with ``sqlite3.database``.  See
+  :py:mod:`salt.cache.sqlite3_cache` for the full list of options.
 * ``consul``, ``redis``, ``etcd``, ``mysql`` — networked backends, useful
   for sharing cache across multiple masters.
 
